  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- interacts with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is a target of multiple compounds, including (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one, [(3S,5aS,6S,7S,9aS)-6-[2-[(5aS,6S,7R,9aS)-7-acetyloxy-2,2,5a,7-tetramethyl-3-oxo-4,5,6,8,9,9a-hexahydrobenzo[b]oxepin-6-yl]ethyl]-7-acetyloxy-2,2,5a,7-tetramethyl-4,5,6,8,9,9a-hexahydro-3H-benzo[b]oxepin-3-yl] acetate, and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. All these compounds share a common target, LAPC4, indicating a potential mechanism of action through the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. The scores from the paths suggest that Nortoxiferine, dihydro- is a promising candidate for targeting LAPC4, as it interacts with a pathway that is a common target of multiple compounds. The evidence supports a relationship between Nortoxiferine, dihydro- and LAPC4 through the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
